  "_readme": [
    "JSON forbids comments, so notes live in this key — iOS ignores unknown top-level keys.",
    "WHY the root exclude: texting the bare 'bizzyu.com' link was opening the app instead of",
    "the website, and the app dead-ends on '/' with a 'Link Not Supported' dialog",
    "(deep_link_service.dart _routeFor, segments.isEmpty). Components are evaluated in order",
    "with FIRST-MATCH-WINS semantics, so the '/' exclude must stay ABOVE the claims.",
    "It matches ONLY the exact root path (any query string — omitting the '?' key means the",
    "query is not considered); every deeper path (/event/*, /p/*, ...) still opens the app.",
    "WHY the /venue/331 and /venue/990227 excludes (2026-10-08): 331 is the Knight Library venue on prod",
    "(990227 on DEV; inert on prod). Its QR is https://knightlibrary.app/v, which the Knight app claims and",
    "which 302s here without the app. A tapped-then-redirected universal link would otherwise bounce the",
    "Knight-themed page into the Bizzy app, so Bizzy must not claim exactly that page. Static on purpose:",
    "the AASA cannot follow the admin app-only toggle. Every other /venue/* still opens Bizzy.",
    "WHY the wholesale /business + /business/* exclude: the ENTIRE /business space is the",
    "web-only operator portal — /business/login, /business/signup, /business/forgot-password,",
    "/business/verify-email, /business/accept-invite and the whole dashboard (analytics,",
    "promo-codes, settings, events, team, marketing…). The app has NO handler for any of it,",
    "so when the space was app-claimed iOS hijacked those links into the app and dead-ended.",
    "We used to patch this path-by-path (accept-invite, then verify-email); this excludes the",
    "whole portal at once so there is ONE source of truth for /business. Both entries are",
    "needed: '/business' matches the bare path, '/business/*' matches everything under it.",
    "The ONE app-relevant path, /business/:id, intentionally stays in the browser too: it",
    "renders the AppInterstitial page, which offers an explicit 'Open in App' button firing",
    "the bizzy://business/:id custom scheme (deep_link_service.dart case 'business'). Same",
    "pattern as /deal and /p — the universal-link claim is dropped and the custom scheme",
    "does the hand-off, so no /business universal-link claim is needed at all.",
    "CACHING CAVEAT: since iOS 14 devices fetch this file via Apple's CDN",
    "(https://app-site-association.cdn-apple.com/a/v1/bizzyu.com), which re-crawls on its own",
    "schedule (typically up to ~1 week), and each device re-evaluates only on app",
    "install/update/reboot cycles. Changes here are NOT live on real phones immediately after",
    "deploy — real-device verification only works on prod bizzyu.com after release."
  ],
